After a few years of nethacking I finally ascended my faithful little
Valkyre over the course of 2 days of playing.

Mistakes were made, and I almost gave up the character about halfway
through. Thankfully I toughed it out.

First big stupid mistake was finding an old bones file on dlvl 12 or so with
a BoH. I picked it up expecting it to be cursed but still would like to have
it around. Then I accidently put it inside of my other BoH that I got from
Sokoban and destroyed both of them, losing a big pile of good scrolls, food,
rings, and other good stuff I was holding onto. At this point I expected to
play until I died from lack of food, or until always being burdened started
to get on my nerves, then quit and start over.

With some stroke of amazing RNG luck I found another BoH on a Troll about 2
dlvls later, and about 90% of the other stuff I lost shortly after that. Not
to mention getting a wish from an altar for my cloak of MR.

Feeling better about the game now, got speed boots, silver dragon scale
mail, gaunts of power, a good half of an AK before I even got to the castle.
The castle went really smoothly with no problems at all clearing it out.

Then big mistake number two happend. WoW chest was locked. Hmmmm, should I
force it? No way to pick anything at this time. Screw it, I'll equip a
dagger (since it seems logical it's hard to destroy a box with a dagger) and
force the box. Bad idea. Destroyed it and broke my WoW. God. Damnit.

Now I'm feeling pretty sad again, but all hope is not lost. Feeling
reckless, I get down to the Valley and start plowing through it. Nothing
spectacular drops and it's pretty uneventful. I go into hell and plow
through it too only coming back up after the second demon to BUC a bunch of
stuff. Vlad comes up, dies painlessly, and I get a second wish from his
altar, which I used on a genocide scroll to get rid of L since my equipment
wasn't too shabby, considering the mistakes made so far, and those liches
were really irking me.

The rest of the game went like clockwork. Found 4 amulets of life saving, an
amulet of magical breathing to ease my nerves in water levels, and a couple
death wands for Rodney. After getting the real amulet ascension wasn't too
painful, bounced around a few times in the maze and 6 instadeaths to Rodney
on the way up.

The first 4 planes were somewhat easier than I expected. I only had 2 gold
detection scrolls that got used on Earth and Air. I paraded everything
around Fire until a monster stepped into the portal for me, and wandered
around Water until I found that one without much trouble. Astral was...
interesting. I never thought I'd be thankful to be surrounded by ants. The
altar was, of course, the last one I checked, but I never had to use an "oLS
or any other heroic measures beyond a few potions of full healing.

And then it was over. Full ascension report is here:
http://chalkdust.org/~discore/ascension.txt

1 genocide and 2 wishes, not bad for a first, especially considering the
mistakes that were made. Quite the learning process. Now my Valks have been
retired and it's time to do a Samauri!



